ap":1,"latitude":"30.609494","longitude":"-96.354382","summary":"","is_starred":"","image_src":"","image_raw":""},{"id":"380606","ts_start":1774882800,"ts_end":1774886400,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/380606-ece-seminar-principled-multimodal-intelligence","title":"ECE Seminar - Principled Multimodal Intelligence for Digital Twins of Science","status":"1","location":"Wisenbaker Engineering Building","has_map":1,"latitude":"30.620771","longitude":"-96.338948","summary":"<p data-path-to-node=\"0\">\n  oin us for a specialized ECE Seminar featuring Dr. Yuhui Zhang from Stanford University, where we will explore the cutting edge of multimodal intelligence. As scientific discovery faces bottlenecks due to human effort and experimental costs, Dr. Zhang presents a vision for \u201cdigital twins of science\u201d\u2014autonomous AI agents capable of retrieving knowledge and validating hypotheses in simulated environments. This session will dive into the principled \u201cscience of AI\u201d approach, addressing fundamental failures in current models like CLIP and GPT to develop more reliable, theoretically grounded solutions for biological data and scientific simulation.\n<\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"1\">\n  <li>\n    <p data-path-to-node=\"1,0,0\">\n      <strong data-path-to-node=\"1,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Date:<\/strong> Monday, March 30th\n    <\/p>\n  <\/li>\n  <li>\n    <p data-path-to-node=\"1,1,0\">\n      <strong data-path-to-node=\"1,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Time:<\/strong> 10:00 a.m. \u2013 11:00 a.m.\n    <\/p>\n  <\/li>\n  <li>\n    <p data-path-to-node=\"1,2,0\">\n      <strong data-path-to-node=\"1,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Location:<\/strong> Wisenbaker 232 &amp; Zoom (<a class=\"ng-star-inserted\" href=\"https:\/\/tamu.zoom.us\/j\/93243208748\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/tamu.zoom.us\/j\/93243208748<\/a>)\n    <\/p>\n  <\/li>\n<\/ul>","is_starred":"","image_src":"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.png","image_raw":"<picture class=\"lw_image\">\n\t<source type=\"image\/webp\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/2x\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.webp 2x, https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/3x\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"\/>\n\t<source type=\"image\/png\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/2x\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.png 2x, https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/3x\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.png 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"\/>\n\t<img src=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.png\" alt=\"Banner graphic with event details.\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/2x\/gid\/63\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,2194,478\/17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM.rev.1774461350.png 2x\" data-max-w=\"2194\" data-max-h=\"478\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"\/>\n<\/picture>\n","image_info":["63","17514_Screenshot_2026-03-25_at_12.55.08PM","png","1","0,0,2194,478","","","","Banner graphic with event details."]},{"id":"380653","ts_start":1774882800,"ts_end":1774895400,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/380653-50-meter","title":"50 Meter","status":"1","location":"","summary":"","is_starred":"","image_src":"","image_raw":""},{"id":"380654","ts_start":1774882800,"ts_end":1774918800,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/380654-outdoor-pool","title":"Outdoor Pool","status":"1","location":"","summary":"","is_starred":"","image_src":"","image_raw":""},{"id":"373896","ts_start":1774886400,"ts_end":1774891800,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/373896-graduate-mentoring-academy-fostering-independence","title":"Graduate Mentoring Academy: Fostering Independence","status":"1","location":"Zoom","summary":"<p>\n  The Graduate Mentoring Academy (GMA) uses the <a href=\"https:\/\/cimerproject.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Center for the Improvement of Mentored Experiences in Research (CIMER)<\/a> resources which includes seven evidence-based mentorship competencies. These Graduate and Professional School workshops, along with efforts from the Center for Teaching Excellence who hosts the <a href=\"https:\/\/gradconnect.tamu.edu\/portal\/fma?tab=home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Faculty Mentoring Academy<\/a> (<strong>for faculty only<\/strong>), work to create a culture of mentoring across our institution.<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  To register, click the link below:<br \/>\n  https:\/\/gradconnect.tamu.edu\/portal\/gma?tab=home\n<\/p>","is_starred":"","image_src":"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/192\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,356,326\/11854_GMA_logo.PNG","image_raw":"<picture class=\"lw_image\">\n\t<source type=\"image\/webp\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/192\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,356,326\/11854_GMA_logo.rev.1706212308.webp 1x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"\/>\n\t<source type=\"image\/png\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/192\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,356,326\/11854_GMA_logo.rev.1706212308.PNG 1x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"\/>\n\t<img src=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/192\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,356,326\/11854_GMA_logo.rev.1706212308.PNG\" alt=\"Graduate Mentoring Academy Logo\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" data-max-w=\"356\" data-max-h=\"326\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"\/>\n<\/picture>\n","image_info":["192","11854_GMA_logo","PNG","1","0,0,356,326","Graduate Mentoring Academy Logo","","",""]},{"id":"374094","ts_start":1774886400,"ts_end":1774891800,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/374094-gma-fostering-independence","title":"GMA | Fostering Independence","status":"1","location":"Zoom","summary":"<strong><strong>Description:<\/strong><\/strong> One of seven competencies offered through the Graduate Mentoring Academy!<br \/>\n<br \/>\nComplete all seven competencies to become a GMA Fellow!<strong><strong><br \/><\/strong><\/strong><br \/>\n<strong>Learning Outcomes<\/strong>: Participants will be able to\u2026<strong><strong><br \/>\n<br \/><\/strong><\/strong>\n<ol>\n  <li>Define independence, its core elements, and how those elements change over the course of a mentoring relationship\n  <\/li>\n  <li>Employ various strategies to build mentee confidence, establish trust, and foster independence\n  <\/li>\n  <li>Identify the benefits and challenges of fostering independence, including the sometimes conflicting goals of fostering independence and achieving grant-funded research objectives\n  <\/li>\n<\/ol><strong><br \/>\nRegister Here<\/strong>: <a href=\"https:\/\/gradconnect.tamu.edu\/register\/?id=62fd7143-985e-4e96-89f5-6154d530f069\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/gradconnect.tamu.edu\/register\/?id=62fd7143-985e-4e96-89f5-6154d530f069<\/a>","is_starred":"","image_src":"https:\/\/calendar.tam